{"id":"3f3e7eea5614d92a","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-df-steenrod-algebra.md","title":"Steenrod Algebra Graded Carrier","display":"df-steenrod-algebra — Steenrod Algebra Graded Carrier","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-steenrod-algebra","aliases":["58-df-steenrod-algebra"],"display":"df-steenrod-algebra — Steenrod Algebra Graded Carrier","depends_on":["[[58-df-cohomology]]","[[58-df-natural-transformation]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-steenrod-algebra"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-steenrod-algebra</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-steenrod-algebra — Steenrod Algebra Graded Carrier"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"03f2d34d9851bee4\" href=\"?note=03f2d34d9851bee4\" title=\"58-df-cohomology\">58-df-cohomology</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"970e2b8779070da0\" href=\"?note=970e2b8779070da0\" title=\"58-df-natural-transformation\">58-df-natural-transformation</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(p\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H_p,\\mathcal C_p,\\mathcal N,\\operatorname{StOp},\\mathcal A_p\\in V\">\\(H_p,\\mathcal C_p,\\mathcal N,\\operatorname{StOp},\\mathcal A_p\\in V\\)</span>, where <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal C_p\">\\(\\mathcal C_p\\)</span> is a fixed set-sized stable test category and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H_p\">\\(H_p\\)</span> is the set code of ordinary mod-<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span> cohomology restricted to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal C_p\">\\(\\mathcal C_p\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Prime}(p)\">\\(\\mathrm{Prime}(p)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H_p=H^*(-;\\mathbb F_p)\\upharpoonright\\mathcal C_p\">\\(H_p=H^*(-;\\mathbb F_p)\\upharpoonright\\mathcal C_p\\)</span> specify that restricted cohomology functor; the unrestricted functor on all spaces is not asserted to be a set.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{StNat}_S(\\eta,H_p,H_p[d])\">\\(\\mathrm{StNat}_S(\\eta,H_p,H_p[d])\\)</span> is the supplied stable-natural-transformation relation on that fixed small presentation, with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H_p[d]^q=H_p^{q+d}\">\\(H_p[d]^q=H_p^{q+d}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SteenrodAlgebra}_S(\\mathcal A_p,p,H_p,\\mathcal N,\\operatorname{StOp})\">\\(\\mathrm{SteenrodAlgebra}_S(\\mathcal A_p,p,H_p,\\mathcal N,\\operatorname{StOp})\\)</span> is the legacy five-place predicate for the underlying graded carrier defined here.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}steenrod\\text{-}algebra}\\vdash \\mathrm{SteenrodAlgebra}_S(\\mathcal A_p,p,H_p,\\mathcal N,\\operatorname{StOp})\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Prime}(p)\\land H_p=H^*(-;\\mathbb F_p)\\upharpoonright\\mathcal C_p\\land\\mathcal N\\in V\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\operatorname{StOp},\\omega,\\mathcal P(\\mathcal N))\\land\\forall d\\in\\omega\\;\\left(\\operatorname{StOp}(d)=\\{\\eta\\in\\mathcal N:\\mathrm{StNat}_S(\\eta,H_p,H_p[d])\\}\\right)\\land\\mathcal A_p=\\bigoplus_{d\\in\\omega}\\operatorname{StOp}(d)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}steenrod\\text{-}algebra}\\vdash \\mathrm{SteenrodAlgebra}_S(\\mathcal A_p,p,H_p,\\mathcal N,\\operatorname{StOp})\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Prime}(p)\\land H_p=H^*(-;\\mathbb F_p)\\upharpoonright\\mathcal C_p\\land\\mathcal N\\in V\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\operatorname{StOp},\\omega,\\mathcal P(\\mathcal N))\\land\\forall d\\in\\omega\\;\\left(\\operatorname{StOp}(d)=\\{\\eta\\in\\mathcal N:\\mathrm{StNat}_S(\\eta,H_p,H_p[d])\\}\\right)\\land\\mathcal A_p=\\bigoplus_{d\\in\\omega}\\operatorname{StOp}(d)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The ambient transformation set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal N\">\\(\\mathcal N\\)</span> and the small source <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal C_p\">\\(\\mathcal C_p\\)</span> are explicit; the object-level function predicate never identifies the unrestricted class functor with a set or uses the proper class <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span> as a codomain.</li>\n<li>This five-place compatibility predicate records only the graded carrier.  The canonical multiplication is composition of stable operations, but its operation graph, unit, and Hopf-algebra structure require a separate structure atom rather than being silently claimed by the carrier equation.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-cohomology","status":"resolved","id":"03f2d34d9851bee4","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cohomology]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-natural-transformation","status":"resolved","id":"970e2b8779070da0","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-natural-transformation]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"p\\in\\mathbb N","display":false},{"tex":"H_p,\\mathcal C_p,\\mathcal N,\\operatorname{StOp},\\mathcal A_p\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal C_p","display":false},{"tex":"H_p","display":false},{"tex":"p","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal C_p","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Prime}(p)","display":false},{"tex":"H_p=H^*(-;\\mathbb F_p)\\upharpoonright\\mathcal C_p","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{StNat}_S(\\eta,H_p,H_p[d])","display":false},{"tex":"H_p[d]^q=H_p^{q+d}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SteenrodAlgebra}_S(\\mathcal A_p,p,H_p,\\mathcal N,\\operatorname{StOp})","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}steenrod\\text{-}algebra}\\vdash \\mathrm{SteenrodAlgebra}_S(\\mathcal A_p,p,H_p,\\mathcal N,\\operatorname{StOp})\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Prime}(p)\\land H_p=H^*(-;\\mathbb F_p)\\upharpoonright\\mathcal C_p\\land\\mathcal N\\in V\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\operatorname{StOp},\\omega,\\mathcal P(\\mathcal N))\\land\\forall d\\in\\omega\\;\\left(\\operatorname{StOp}(d)=\\{\\eta\\in\\mathcal N:\\mathrm{StNat}_S(\\eta,H_p,H_p[d])\\}\\right)\\land\\mathcal A_p=\\bigoplus_{d\\in\\omega}\\operatorname{StOp}(d)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathcal N","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal C_p","display":false},{"tex":"V","display":false}],"bytes":2184,"backlinks":[{"id":"12ff4099e35b4ab6","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathcal A_p$ (mod-$p$ Steenrod 代数, see [[../batch20/58-df-steenrod-algebra.md]])"},{"id":"f249216f43ced95c","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1223","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-steenrod-algebra.md|58-df-steenrod-algebra]]（batch20）"}],"outgoing":["03f2d34d9851bee4","970e2b8779070da0"